// Auto-generated from legacy HTML by scripts/extract-pages.py
export const title = "Geutebr&uuml;ck Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Geutebr&uuml;ck Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 104507 or greater.</li>\n<li>Geutebr&uuml;ck G-Core SDK 10.0.0.288 or greater.</li>\n<li>Geutebr&uuml;ck PluginLoader 1.6.0 or greater.</li>\n<li>Geutebr&uuml;ck GCoreWebApi 2.0.17 or greater.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<p>AIBridge receives RTSP (Real-Time Streaming Protocol) video streams directly from IP cameras. It analyzes the received video in real time to detect objects (e.g. people, vehicles) and generates events based on configured rules (e.g. intrusion detection, license plate recognition).</p>\n<p>The video stream &ndash; now carrying AI analysis overlays such as object bounding boxes and zone displays &ndash; along with the detected event information (e.g. \"Intrusion detected on channel 1\"), is then transmitted to the Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS. The Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS, via the AIBridge plugin, receives this annotated video and event data and integrates it with core VMS functions such as live monitoring, event search, and alarms.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 300\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"220\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"215\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <rect x=\"330\" y=\"20\" width=\"200\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f2f3f6\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\"/>\n  <text x=\"430\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#7a4f10\" font-weight=\"700\">GEUTEBR&Uuml;CK</text>\n  <rect x=\"360\" y=\"190\" width=\"150\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#0b0f19\"/>\n  <text x=\"435\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"430\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"435\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrGB)\" marker-start=\"url(#arrGB)\"/>\n  <text x=\"450\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7a4f10\" font-weight=\"700\">AI Event<tspan x=\"450\" dy=\"14\">&amp; annotated Video</tspan></text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrGB\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#e0a94c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>IP cameras stream RTSP video to AIBridge; AIBridge analyzes it and sends the AI event and annotated video to Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS via the AIBridge plugin</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<p>Seamless event integration between AIBridge and Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS requires configuration on both systems. This section explains each step.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.1 Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS Configuration</h3>\n<p>This section explains how to add the AIBridge device to the Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS and configure the events for integration.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.1.1 Download and Add the AIBridge Plugin</h4>\n<p>Several preliminary steps are required to use the AIBridge Plugin in Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS. First, ensure that G-Core SDK, Plugin Loader, and G-Core Web Api are installed. Next, add the AIBridge Plugin to the Geutebr&uuml;ck PluginLoader.</p>\n<p>Download the <code>AIBridgeGeutebr&uuml;ckPlugin_v0.x.x_.zip</code> file.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. The AIBridge Plugin can be obtained by contacting the Indo AI sales team.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Open <strong>Services</strong> in Windows. In the Services list, find the <strong>GEUTEBR&Uuml;CK PluginLoader</strong> service and stop it.</p>\n<p>On the PC where the Geutebr&uuml;ck PluginLoader is installed, unzip the downloaded AIBridgePlugin zip file into <code>C:\\Program Files\\Geutebrueck\\PluginLoader\\plugins</code>. After unzipping, open the AIBridgePlugin folder and confirm that its contents are structured correctly.</p>\n<p>In the Services list, find the GEUTEBR&Uuml;CK PluginLoader service again and start it.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Tip. Ensure that the service port (default: 8888) is not blocked by your firewall.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Finally, open the Plugin Loader interface and verify that the AIBridge Plugin is listed. If it appears, the plugin has been successfully registered with Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.1.2 Adding the Device</h4>\n<p>To view the annotated video analyzed by AIBridge in the VMS, you must register AIBridge as a device.</p>\n<p>Navigate to the Plugin Loader and click <strong>Connect</strong>. Launch the Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin Loader, go to the <strong>DEVICES</strong> tab, and click <strong>Add Device</strong>.</p>\n<p>From the <strong>Plugin Type</strong> dropdown, select <strong>AIBridge Plugin</strong>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">Add Device</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Plugin Type</span><select disabled><option>AIBridge Plugin</option></select>\n      <span>Device Name</span><input value=\"AI Bridge - Lobby\" disabled>\n      <span>IP</span><input value=\"192.168.101.10\" disabled>\n      <span>Username</span><input value=\"admin\" disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input disabled>\n      <span>HTTP(S) Port</span><input value=\"8443\" disabled>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Connect + Configure</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Add Device &ndash; enter the AIBridge device's connection information</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p>Enter the connection information for the AIBridge device:</p>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Device Name</strong> &ndash; the name displayed when managing the device in G-Set.</li>\n<li><strong>IP</strong> &ndash; the IP address of the AIBridge device.</li>\n<li><strong>Username / Password</strong> &ndash; the administrator credentials used to access the AIBridge web interface.</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP(S) Port</strong> &ndash; the web access port for AIBridge (default: 8443).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Click <strong>Connect + Configure</strong>. A green icon appears upon successful connection, and 8 channels are automatically populated in the Sensor tab below. For easier management, you can rename each channel with a more descriptive name (e.g. Main Entrance, Restricted Area, Vault Hallway).</p>\n<p>Once configuration is complete, click the <strong>Save</strong> button in the upper-right corner to save the changes to the Geutebr&uuml;ck server.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.1.3 Event and Action Settings</h4>\n<p>After registering the device, add and configure the events in Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS that will be linked to the events generated by AIBridge.</p>\n<p>Launch Geutebr&uuml;ck G-Set and go to the <strong>Event</strong> tab. Add a new event and configure it as follows. Repeat this process for each AIBridge channel you wish to integrate.</p>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Active</strong> &ndash; check the box to activate.</li>\n<li><strong>Retrigger mode</strong> &ndash; select <strong>Start new instance</strong> (this ensures each recurrence of the same event is logged as a new instance).</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. The <strong>Event type ID</strong> automatically assigned upon creation is used later to map channels in the AIBridge Action Handler settings.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Go to the <strong>Alarm</strong> tab, check <strong>Active</strong>, and add the camera channel that will receive this event (the AIBridge channel registered in section 2.1.2) to the <strong>Media channels</strong> field.</p>\n<p>Once all settings are configured, click the Save icon in the upper-left corner to save the configuration.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 AIBridge Configuration</h3>\n<p>This section explains how to create AI analysis rules and configure event forwarding to the Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS via the AIBridge web interface.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.2.1 Adding AI Apps</h4>\n<p>Log in to the AIBridge web interface and click <strong>Explore AI Apps</strong> from the left-side menu. Select the desired AI feature. AIBridge provides over 60 AI applications for various use cases &ndash; see the full app list at the <a href=\"https://indoai.com/goods/catalog?page=1&searchMode=catalog&category=c0006&per=40&sorting=ranking&filter_display=lattice&code=0006\">catalog link</a>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. This guide uses the LPR app as an example.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Click <strong>Add Rule</strong> to create a new analysis rule, then click <strong>Add</strong> under Event Setting. Define a detection zone on the video feed, configure detailed conditions such as sensitivity and object types, and click <strong>Apply</strong> to save the rule.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:18px;font-size:15px;\">2.2.2 Action Handler Settings</h4>\n<p>Configure an action to send event information to the Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS whenever an event is triggered by an AI app rule.</p>\n<p>In the settings screen for the newly created AI app rule, click <strong>Add</strong> under Action Setting. From the <strong>Action Type</strong> dropdown, select <strong>Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin</strong>, then click <strong>Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin Action Add</strong>.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<p>Click <strong>Edit</strong> and enter the Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin connection information:</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"modal-mock\">\n  <div class=\"modal-head\">Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin</div>\n  <div class=\"modal-body\">\n    <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n      <span>Host</span><input value=\"192.168.101.15\" disabled>\n      <span>Username</span><input disabled>\n      <span>Password</span><input disabled>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"margin-top:8px;color:var(--green);font-size:12px;\">&#9679; Connected</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"modal-foot\"><span class=\"btn small\">Cancel</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Login</span> <span class=\"btn small primary\">Apply</span></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin connection settings</figcaption>\n</div>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li><strong>Host</strong> &ndash; the IP address of the Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin server.</li>\n<li><strong>Username / Password</strong> &ndash; the administrator credentials for the Geutebr&uuml;ck G-Core server.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. Video transmission is not supported in 16-channel mode and dynamic view settings.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Click <strong>Login</strong>. The status should change to <strong>Connected</strong>. If it remains Disconnected, verify your credentials and network settings.</p>\n\n<h5 style=\"margin-top:16px;font-size:14px;\">Channel Mapping</h5>\n<p>Click <strong>Mapping</strong>. In each channel's input field, enter the corresponding Event type ID assigned in section 2.1.3. For example, to link events from AIBridge's Channel 1 to the \"AIBridge Event1\" you registered in Geutebr&uuml;ck VMS (which was assigned Event type ID \"7\"), enter <code>7</code> into the Channel 1 input field.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>AIBridge Channel</th><th>Geutebr&uuml;ck Event Type ID</th></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 1</td><td><input value=\"7\" disabled style=\"width:80px;\"></td></tr>\n<tr><td>CH 2</td><td><input value=\"8\" disabled style=\"width:80px;\"></td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. Mapping is managed per action handler. To register multiple AI events for a single channel, register a separate action handler for each AI App &ndash; see section 4.2.</p>\n</div>\n<p>After entering the Event Type IDs, click <strong>Events update</strong> to display the mapped events.</p>\n\n<h5 style=\"margin-top:16px;font-size:14px;\">Description Message</h5>\n<p>Click <strong>Description Set</strong>. Since this guide uses LPR as an example, select <strong>Basic Information + LPR</strong>, click <strong>Use</strong>, then click <strong>Submit</strong> at the bottom right. The message configured here can be checked in the Event List of Geutebr&uuml;ck G-View.</p>\n<p>Once configuration is complete, click the <strong>Test</strong> button to send a test event from AIBridge to the Geutebr&uuml;ck server. If the test event is sent successfully, it appears in the event list of Geutebr&uuml;ck's G-View monitoring client.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<p>After completing all configurations, you can verify the integration in the Geutebr&uuml;ck G-View client.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.1 Live</h3>\n<p>Check the live video feed from the AIBridge channels in G-View. Verify that the AI analysis overlays, such as object bounding boxes or configured detection zones, are displayed on top of the live video.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.2 Event List</h3>\n<p>Trigger a condition that matches the configured AI app rule (e.g. a vehicle entering an LPR detection zone). Confirm that the event is received in real time in the G-View Event List.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:700;\">The meaning of each event field is as follows:</p>\n<ul class=\"steps\" style=\"margin:0;\">\n<li><strong>textA</strong> &ndash; the message set in the action handler.</li>\n<li><strong>textB</strong> &ndash; the AIBridge device name.</li>\n<li><strong>textC</strong> &ndash; the channel name.</li>\n<li><strong>textD</strong> &ndash; the event name.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2>4. FAQ</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.1 LPR App Usage Example: Configuring the Geutebr&uuml;ck Event List Text</h3>\n<p>This section explains how to use the LPR (License Plate Recognition) app within AIBridge to configure TextA, the message displayed in the Geutebr&uuml;ck Event List.</p>\n<p>In AIBridge's Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin settings, TextA corresponds to the <strong>Description</strong> field. By using the LPR app, you can set up vehicle groups and manage entry/exit movements, reflecting this information in the Description field and ultimately in TextA on Geutebr&uuml;ck's Event List.</p>\n<p>To manage vehicle movements, define the recognition zones and the movement direction. In the LPR Event Setting, configure the specific zone you'll use to manage vehicle entry and exit, and specify the directional parameters in the Object Movement Direction section.</p>\n<p>You can set up groups to categorize specific license plates (e.g. \"Bank Staff,\" \"Bank Executive,\" \"VIP\"). In the LPR app, go to LP Management and select the Group tab, then create and name the groups you want to manage.</p>\n<p>Go to License Plate management, register the desired license plates, and select the appropriate group each plate belongs to.</p>\n<p>The final step is to build the custom message that appears in the Geutebr&uuml;ck Event List. Navigate to the Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin settings and click <strong>Description Set</strong> to create the Description Message. In the Token section, register the following system variables (tokens):</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Token</th><th>Represents</th></tr>\n<tr><td>EVENT META1</td><td>Vehicle License Plate Number</td></tr>\n<tr><td>EVENT META2</td><td>Group Information (e.g. \"Staff\")</td></tr>\n<tr><td>EVENT META3</td><td>Entry/Exit Information (e.g. \"Entry,\" \"Exit\")</td></tr>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>In the Editable Box, you can freely combine text and these tokens to create your custom message. Example message composition: <code>[LP Number] &ndash; [Group] &ndash; [In/Out Status]</code>, built from the tokens <code>[EVENT META1] &ndash; [EVENT META2] &ndash; [EVENT META3]</code>.</p>\n<p>Once all settings are complete and saved, you can verify the custom message in the Geutebr&uuml;ck Event List.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">4.2 How to Configure Multiple AI Events on a Single Channel</h3>\n<p>If you want to register multiple events &ndash; such as Intrusion Detection and LPR &ndash; on a single video channel in AIBridge, follow these steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>Add</strong> under Action Setting, then select <strong>Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin</strong>, and click <strong>Geutebr&uuml;ck Plugin Action Add</strong>.</li>\n<li>Set the <strong>Action Preset Name</strong> to distinguish between the different AI apps (e.g. LPR, Intrusion), and enter the Plugin Loader Server details along with the remaining information.\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note. Only one Plugin Loader Server can be registered, and communication is limited to a single Geutebr&uuml;ck Server.</p>\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Apply</strong>. An action named \"LPR\" is created. Check the corresponding box and click <strong>Apply</strong> again.</li>\n<li>Select another AI app (e.g. Intrusion Detection), create a zone for it, then create an additional Geutebr&uuml;ck action handler. Don't change the Plugin Loader Server information, since only one server can be used.</li>\n<li>Once setup is complete, select the newly created Intrusion Detection action and click <strong>Apply</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>With all settings complete, whenever an Intrusion Detection or LPR event occurs on the same channel, both events are successfully transmitted to the Geutebr&uuml;ck system.</p>\n\n<h2>5. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>v1.00 &ndash; Initial document creation.</li>\n<li>v1.10 &ndash; Added section 4, FAQ.</li>\n<li>v1.20 &ndash; Modified section 2.2.2, Action Handler Settings.</li>\n<li>v1.30 &ndash; Granular breakdown and comprehensive update of document content, including UI details.</li>\n<li>v1.40 &ndash; Added section 4.2 (how to configure multiple AI events) and updated the primary manual example to LPR.</li>\n</ul>";
